{"name":"Mana Tree","hex":"#4f7942","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mana","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Power, prestige; specifically, a form of supernatural energy in Polynesian religion that inheres in things or people. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Magical energy."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of mina (“ancient unit of weight or currency”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mana"},{"term":"tree","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A perennial woody plant taller and larger than a shrub with a wooden trunk and, at some distance from the ground, having leaves and branches.","Any other plant (such as a large shrub or herb) that is reminiscent of the above in form and size."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To chase (an animal or person) up a tree.","To place in a tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tree"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mana (series)","blocks":[{"text":"The Mana series, known in Japan as Seiken Densetsu , is an action role-playing game series created by Koichi Ishii, with development formerly from Square, and is currently owned by Square Enix. The series began in 1991 as Final Fantasy Adventure, a Game Boy handheld side story to Square's flagship franchise Final Fantasy. The Final Fantasy elements were subsequently dropped starting with the second installment, Secret of Mana, in order to become its own series. It has grown to include games of various genres within the fictional world of Mana, with recurring stories involving a world tree, its associated holy sword, and the fight against forces that would steal their power. Several character designs, creatures, and musical themes reappear frequently."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mana_(series)","wikidata":"Q587964"},{"title":"Tree","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a tree is a perennial plant with an elongated stem, or trunk, usually supporting branches and leaves. In some usages, the definition of a tree may be narrower, e.g., including only woody plants with secondary growth, only plants that are usable for timber, or only plants above a specified height. Wider definitions include taller palms, tree ferns, bananas, and bamboos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree","wikidata":"Q10884"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/72/Ringmenu.png/330px-Ringmenu.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/72/Ringmenu.png/330px-Ringmenu.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Mana series' Ring Command menu (from Trials of Mana)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARingmenu.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e2/Mana_Tree.jpg/250px-Mana_Tree.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e2/Mana_Tree.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e2/Mana_Tree.jpg/250px-Mana_Tree.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Artwork of the Mana Tree, from Children of Mana","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMana_Tree.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/04/Rabite_Mana.png/250px-Rabite_Mana.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/04/Rabite_Mana.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/04/